newReturnSelfT -- SEQ 509: newReturnT's RT-7 in its own process. Every new-road call instruct takes the callee of the LAST
call built (pre-existing, measured on trunk SEQ 509, not chased), so a self-call cannot share a process with another
action's call. Same pairing as newReturnT: n built on the new road (nlNew), o on the old (nlOld), the control.

RP    road proof: new [ 7 ], old [     7 ].
RT-7  a self-call that returns at depth (newLocalT's AL-3 shape, read by value): a declared counter (2) counts down, each
      level returns its own r7 and the level above prints it: 0 1, then rx reads 2. A shared local would print 0 0 / 0.
